      "writtenOn": "2024-01-11T04:45:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Interface names are often error prone because the same interface name can have multiple ifindices over the course of its lifetime. This is particularly true for tun interfaces which are created/destroyed. If interface indices are available, it\u0027s better to use those. Unfortunately most of our code uses names so this may not be possible. But if it\u0027s possible you might want to try to convert names to indices \"on input\" and use the indices in this code.\n\nIf you already have some mapping between interface name and index, then you could convert this into a SparseIntArray from physical index to virtual index.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 135,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 135,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "5fbf5b3c8499f8a36f557815f9b91b9977ddb762",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
